dsstack contains original skills and Python tooling by doublesharp.

Workflow ideas adapted from:
- t3dotgg/tstack, MIT. Bounded review, scoped re-review, and explicit PR ownership.
- obra/superpowers, MIT. Behavioral RED/GREEN, root-cause debugging, resumable progress, and skill validation.
- cursor/plugins pstack, MIT, Lauren Tan. Practical regression checks, substantiated reviews, and retry-safe operations.
- cloudflare/security-audit-skill, MIT, Cloudflare, Inc. Source-grounded security findings, dependency/release trust boundaries, and bounded local validation in optional ds-security.

Retained upstream license notices are in licenses/. Exact source revisions and
file hashes are recorded in upstreams.lock.json. The 2026-10-31 revision also
draws on published guidance from Anthropic, OpenAI, and individual practitioners.
The skills copy no text from those sources; docs/provenance.md links them and
quotes short excerpts. No upstream installer, hook, runtime, or downloaded code
is executed by dsstack.
